    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15080" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ecclēsĭastĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκλησιαστικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			Church</i>, <i>ecclesiastical.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pax,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pudic. 22</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ecclesiasticus</span></b> , i, m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A church officer</i>, Cod. Th. 1, 3,
			22.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The name of the Book of Sirach</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 6, 2, 31</span></i>.</div>
